  - **(B3-1) S1 cannot test a floor.** The update (`e5_b3.py` l.~100) is gW = PᵀPWA11 − PᵀWA21 with a copy target. Its columns stay in range(W) whenever P maps range(W) into itself, and P = p0 I plus updates R Wᵀ keeps that. So the rank of W cannot rise, exactly; the theory note calls it "Range invariance (exact)". The floor/reseeding account is therefore excluded by construction in this model. A re-escape event under the code's definition (alive, then below THR = 0.05, then above) can come only from noise fluctuations of a still-nonzero singular value around THR, not from reseeding.
    - The exit rule "A failed S1 or S2 favours the floor account and is stated as such in N3" is therefore wrong.
    - "What it supports" ("SGD noise does not reseed collapsed directions") is a property of this linear model with a copy target, not an empirical finding about SGD.
    - Needed before the held-out run: register S1 as a consistency check of the exact invariance, with the floor account named as excluded by the model; give the failure reading as THR-crossing fluctuations; scope N3's clause to models with this invariance. Out of scope are an EMA target that lags, additive noise such as augmentation or label noise, and nonlinear layers.
    - The JSON's S1 wording ("below THR at a check and above it at a later check") omits the code's requirement that the value was alive before. That should be aligned.
  - **(B3-2) S2 can be decided by round-off.** S2 compares median log10(dead / top) levels across B, but `dead_level` has no float64 round-off guard, unlike the slope, which uses ROUND = 1e-13. Dev already sits at −15.4 for B = 2 (round-off). If both B = 2 and B = 32 reach round-off in some η cell, the strict order is decided by SVD round-off, not dynamics. Needed: declare before the held-out run how levels at or below ROUND × top are read (for example as tied, and the order read on the dead log-slope).

